#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068370 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1de6657-82b1-5bcb-b8cc-fd2629d31faa" :question/math-academy-id "e-10832" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' = \\dfrac {x^2}{y}.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}y^2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}x^3 + C.\n$$\n\nWe can express the solution in the form $y = y(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = 2C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068371 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23d66cc8-8e5a-5a33-a7a1-c43f5facdcbc" :question/math-academy-id "e-10833" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' + 2xy = 0$ for $y\\neq 0.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln \\vert y \\vert = -x^2 + C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y = y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = e^C$  and $K > 0.$ \n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ke^{-x^2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068372 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32040154-373e-5a10-a460-1d17f6989da0" :question/math-academy-id "e-10849" :question/problem "Given that $x,y \\geq 0,$ separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\sqrt{2xy}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{g(y)} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} =  \\sqrt{2x} \\cdot  \\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{y}} \\cdot \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\sqrt{2x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068374 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d53c6172-978d-57c7-b1f0-e56e892e48a9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10997" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n    =\n    \\dfrac{x}{y}.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+2K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C= 2K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ny^2 = x^2 + C .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d9c51e-3a0e-5bc4-b172-8b6583ceb715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}+x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290008} {:answer/id #uuid "d90487e7-735b-56e9-bcca-77c3b5f97cef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290009} {:answer/id #uuid "94b1405d-06d4-582a-9313-ba2f85b9a4cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290010} {:answer/id #uuid "861f4686-f4df-53f0-ad82-ef638f2ee62b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290011} {:answer/id #uuid "0891ba75-1555-5a7d-9417-da806933b1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0891ba75-1555-5a7d-9417-da806933b1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290012} :answer-field/id #uuid "859b6ae2-bd80-505f-a258-6fe94803aaa5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f1d7bb9-17fc-5ea6-b46c-64a6f08a7c91" :question/math-academy-id "q-14253" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+2{y}^{2}x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}+2{y}^{2}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(1+2x) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =x+{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{y}={x}^{2}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7670e8de-1326-5f9f-9a9d-5c3b357abb06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290015} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d89319-5dec-5a29-9fe6-e628188e6e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290016} {:answer/id #uuid "f58425b4-83a3-5c4e-9e6e-d3207b2fd215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290017} {:answer/id #uuid "f4066a96-3273-532a-996b-0641e0162c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290018} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd03651-0481-5063-9444-cfc70c0eb94e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8d89319-5dec-5a29-9fe6-e628188e6e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290016} :answer-field/id #uuid "74271519-b18b-56ea-ac51-74907b249227" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f395e372-17f7-5405-8db5-57998e5659ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-154361" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aed1cbca-9e55-5892-af1d-df1ff1509101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\arctan y = x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065819} {:answer/id #uuid "fef1e70c-da45-5a86-85ab-5b4aac412df1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan y = x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065820} {:answer/id #uuid "2a8469a6-2ebc-5595-a41a-d5fd323f541a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin y = x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065821} {:answer/id #uuid "494bc739-0e89-510d-aed4-e0553dd43d5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\arccos y = x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065822} {:answer/id #uuid "5291991b-f6ee-55f2-8bdd-941a8a475bc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\arcsin y = x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5291991b-f6ee-55f2-8bdd-941a8a475bc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\arcsin y = x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065823} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdbc7d89-cef8-5720-be51-44d59b581954" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc5a6535-55d7-58bf-9da3-473b544214d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-154367" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\,$ for $\\,|y|<1.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y & =x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y=x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ed89cd4-db12-5c49-ae2a-17aea3d08188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290022} {:answer/id #uuid "56616332-794d-51ea-af06-084f11a43f74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290023} {:answer/id #uuid "deb58696-83e2-5555-817f-215602279b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290024} {:answer/id #uuid "1189f080-3a6e-5660-afd7-8cc50119a3d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290025} {:answer/id #uuid "48746e41-b515-521b-a7e0-237e5b4d84ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1189f080-3a6e-5660-afd7-8cc50119a3d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290025} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ab8e971-cfb0-51b3-b12f-7a645d1412c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a72cd73-068f-5aa7-91b3-dbc11c176b22" :question/math-academy-id "q-154373" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2{y}^{3/2}}{3} & =\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+K \\\\ {y}^{3/2} & ={x}^{3/2}+C \\\\ \\sqrt{{y}^{3}} & =\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{3K}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9372fe8a-9fe7-5b4d-bda4-372a083ddca5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x + 1}{x} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = y^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065831} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f4abee-366d-5610-8fb5-d09a162b2c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{y^{2}}{x + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065832} {:answer/id #uuid "f7f10af7-a270-5ce4-a424-4307343938cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 1) \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = xy^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065833} {:answer/id #uuid "714ca07c-83ac-5ede-be6f-c4ae92b77715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{x}{x + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065834} {:answer/id #uuid "75b0eb6d-0154-58d2-9a2d-8276d5ffdc36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y^{2}} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{x}{x + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75b0eb6d-0154-58d2-9a2d-8276d5ffdc36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y^{2}} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{x}{x + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065835} :answer-field/id #uuid "65e4bc99-ff97-5d84-85c3-18160f4ad8ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8143064d-a592-5c44-b653-c218df46c5ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-154678" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{x+1}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(\\frac{x}{x+1})\\cdot {y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c36598d-5ca9-592d-8401-cc7e45dd6869" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290029} {:answer/id #uuid "33a871e5-40f0-5092-9d15-573dc419bb72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290030} {:answer/id #uuid "5a54976d-a092-5a81-b6c8-483f01ad8c9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290031} {:answer/id #uuid "02323412-dfad-5f89-b55c-865d24ea1861" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290032} {:answer/id #uuid "1151795e-7510-5ff9-b975-a5119a5cd670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{1/\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02323412-dfad-5f89-b55c-865d24ea1861" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290032} :answer-field/id #uuid "af49c7fd-847c-5683-90d2-b1ed7c6bd5f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c927b6a4-3cff-5587-a42a-b3d1d59c6570" :question/math-academy-id "q-158010" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,{y}^{′}-y=0$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $|x|<1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,{y}^{′}-y & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc369823-8d5e-5fb4-9843-2b1db974b760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290036} {:answer/id #uuid "c9faa650-8742-503d-9056-30ec4f094de3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(\\sqrt[3]{x}+C)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290037} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2de853-237e-5dd0-a350-1dc2b509ce7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{2x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290038} {:answer/id #uuid "79e4646a-be4c-528c-835d-efc1f7784fef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290039} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb6361a-1bcc-517b-bdc8-ffd88e20b18e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{3}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc369823-8d5e-5fb4-9843-2b1db974b760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290036} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e81955a-cb56-51ae-900b-0a206645fb7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84edc4b8-8df5-5463-b957-9bbf44dd553d" :question/math-academy-id "q-158012" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{3{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{3{y}^{2}} \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1f8f621-d93c-502b-8675-9db1faf29bd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290043} {:answer/id #uuid "602ddebc-9875-542b-bfb3-35cd8e105d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290044} {:answer/id #uuid "0af79cfa-50c7-5ccc-a34a-b105fb640511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290045} {:answer/id #uuid "ebde7d7b-7708-5f47-93ea-fb66358a313d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290046} {:answer/id #uuid "fa647dc1-91e8-5f0d-b7b8-bea8690818ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0af79cfa-50c7-5ccc-a34a-b105fb640511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290045} :answer-field/id #uuid "92306383-ac9e-5217-8c24-3963a5997891" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0b2f5622-0ea4-5d24-ae30-e39b34ff5b26" :question/math-academy-id "q-158013" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee68888-dbb2-5ca0-80cb-6c60f3bd0155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290050} {:answer/id #uuid "8545cda7-dff1-5955-a591-94cf845e0016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290051} {:answer/id #uuid "56c46223-d9f3-5e31-ae79-b5c2146f681f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290052} {:answer/id #uuid "f20b16d2-b13d-5314-a9d2-801a551d4be7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290053} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb5bcff-df86-512b-b9bb-07304f9b353c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56c46223-d9f3-5e31-ae79-b5c2146f681f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290052} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcf3d22a-e0e4-5060-a63d-8decf4600d8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290049}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca7be506-83fc-5b5f-8d5e-a2372dca466d" :question/math-academy-id "q-158014" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9757084a-a1cb-5337-8c57-7da0bc015462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290057} {:answer/id #uuid "f735ef79-5ba0-5023-a246-c0663599772a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290058} {:answer/id #uuid "172f8f2b-c0b9-5a41-85f7-f2d56f70e93b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290059} {:answer/id #uuid "294c8552-fe67-5424-b605-b6c69d212878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290060} {:answer/id #uuid "d52a641f-c4ed-562e-aac2-3ea6484ec8f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{1/\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "294c8552-fe67-5424-b605-b6c69d212878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290060} :answer-field/id #uuid "942851af-e04d-5857-96eb-cf68d0cf348e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8d22cbc-8a07-502c-a919-a1d79d8cef97" :question/math-academy-id "q-158016" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $|x|<1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ed99773-2ede-5506-a96a-89f0d0aff279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290064} {:answer/id #uuid "7b099e5b-6665-5fdf-8e1c-607c78e6992a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290065} {:answer/id #uuid "fa61f554-9f61-5fa7-b712-5fc1e11b86fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290066} {:answer/id #uuid "e135b769-e946-5c21-b366-d3cd5f273fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290067} {:answer/id #uuid "9bea2cb2-cb4a-53e7-b613-47b5e320c895" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b099e5b-6665-5fdf-8e1c-607c78e6992a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290065} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd85d616-f3b0-5b82-8e03-93399be05b4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43663e7b-df9d-5b87-a219-ac4ecaba337f" :question/math-academy-id "q-158022" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\cdot y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d2f253e-ed6f-54ad-8d73-f9bb2ce95c30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290071} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7246a9-edf9-5d49-918e-7561f172aa68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+x{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290072} {:answer/id #uuid "1bd12d81-b9c1-56e2-b3c6-41f3a0992daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+x{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290073} {:answer/id #uuid "987e51c1-8181-5439-941c-056338351839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290074} {:answer/id #uuid "91bcca5c-4cc5-5792-8944-abcdcc89cf63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91bcca5c-4cc5-5792-8944-abcdcc89cf63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290075} :answer-field/id #uuid "d82787ca-8609-5785-a921-cc614e54db00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c84cfba-4095-5b52-b06f-553c982d22ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-158023" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x+x{y}^{2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\\cdot (1+{y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290076 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200ff40b-c483-5511-ada4-9962f1c23d0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290078} {:answer/id #uuid "549aa129-3c38-5279-aaf0-8fc6677cb0c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290079} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6f447c-5fc8-5dfe-8140-683e78c870c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290080} {:answer/id #uuid "91acb97c-fd3b-5dfa-afb4-225be15bbf45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290081} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba46a08-ea30-56e0-baae-58f6e1ba67d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ba46a08-ea30-56e0-baae-58f6e1ba67d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290082} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ebceda-4b19-5c0e-a39b-5accbe931e11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb5bb3ab-6532-5577-9047-8f7af02e49c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-158026" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290083 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df758d0e-cfd9-5633-9937-06734f1dadad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290085} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5e4add-8474-56c5-b9f1-74138be46566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290086} {:answer/id #uuid "e1200b00-76c5-56c4-9805-fe8cd02cdea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290087} {:answer/id #uuid "250598c9-e4a7-528c-b6e1-4d20fc85fffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290088} {:answer/id #uuid "026d5bf6-a7c1-5e06-8422-0743ce837bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\text{ }\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad5e4add-8474-56c5-b9f1-74138be46566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290086} :answer-field/id #uuid "95e320e5-1eb4-517c-9bd9-97745a54c3a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1966b7ec-9eb0-519d-bc45-7210a4a3667d" :question/math-academy-id "q-158027" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot {y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bae4517-ca75-59cb-a32f-b2a2a2c2eaa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290092} {:answer/id #uuid "0aeecf5d-5702-513e-801c-5c126e01c8a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290093} {:answer/id #uuid "17ce1359-aa2a-5472-9c96-f2901f6cba5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{ }y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290094} {:answer/id #uuid "222d92b3-2dcd-5344-b8b0-8d766efd687a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290095} {:answer/id #uuid "201dba49-412a-5f39-a491-3eaaf266d447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "201dba49-412a-5f39-a491-3eaaf266d447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290096} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0239e82-ea6b-51fb-b67b-3105cf1e47e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "575d49f3-8bd3-5463-bab9-a94f8bc81fb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-158035" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y & ={x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d27ee6c2-1b6d-59c4-8c21-6fb69aefd4eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290099} {:answer/id #uuid "0f1386bf-6e21-59b5-99bb-48e26b2dd99c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290100} {:answer/id #uuid "025c3afe-0e1a-545c-93fc-afb7a94a47e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290101} {:answer/id #uuid "2fcabdb7-87f0-56d9-943a-24323eb049d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290102} {:answer/id #uuid "0c1a8c2a-acbb-54f7-810d-1ac1c25cb446" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d27ee6c2-1b6d-59c4-8c21-6fb69aefd4eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290099} :answer-field/id #uuid "b36339ba-910f-5f2b-aeb8-30257127d182" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a9f1df5-0abe-52e3-bf22-4b38e70bcd85" :question/math-academy-id "q-158117" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "128eee03-ebf6-5e0f-a12c-86ca6152676d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290106} {:answer/id #uuid "4bda40f0-2d83-59e6-8f7b-7ba05cf47032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290107} {:answer/id #uuid "61da996c-429e-5771-9273-3176fc625092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290108} {:answer/id #uuid "07c6ebfc-e491-5570-a132-4f1f7d478f38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290109} {:answer/id #uuid "f72e1a12-1c41-5fc1-b88e-073808038329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07c6ebfc-e491-5570-a132-4f1f7d478f38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290109} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3632192-c66e-50c5-801e-6d1652a6c0f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76330838-614a-5353-8d92-b88e4c3411af" :question/math-academy-id "q-3850" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x{e}^{-y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{e}^{y}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b77b1bab-d61a-51fd-ac76-46d237d3c984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{6x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290113} {:answer/id #uuid "59f85b27-4e41-5a41-960b-ad9a37fd1329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{3{x}^{2}+2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290114} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8bb634-72c0-55c9-92da-f5d7e725d536" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290115} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb55016-963a-5440-ad69-b4690e203631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290116} {:answer/id #uuid "42d289aa-6bdd-5d3a-906e-71a6468e02c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f8bb634-72c0-55c9-92da-f5d7e725d536" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290115} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d7defa0-0bd3-5dba-a9b1-ce70b28f05df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e1ecad53-dd2a-50f5-9cf7-3133c20315a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-79663" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-2xy=3{x}^{2}y$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-2xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}y+2xy \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(3{x}^{2}+2x)y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83886acf-1c8e-5960-b6ee-e7830ed74739" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290120} {:answer/id #uuid "1fb29469-b4cf-5fa4-9b43-729d593893b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{C}{2{x}^{3}+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290121} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e52c87-c4b3-52a7-8ff6-ffd53d74f1fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290122} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ab7321-4111-5db9-9f25-55c51a7d43f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290123} {:answer/id #uuid "18a72a28-9a43-5b76-a889-40e9df5aefb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5ab7321-4111-5db9-9f25-55c51a7d43f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290123} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ceb3d60-5583-5261-82e7-277a1667cf86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09d456a1-9fef-5540-85ee-2f11d2f0e40e" :question/math-academy-id "q-79664" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-{y}^{2}=6{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-{y}^{2} & =6{x}^{2}{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{y}^{2} & =6{x}^{2}{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(6{x}^{2}+1){y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (6{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =2{x}^{3}+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{y}=2{x}^{3}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bde6803c-41d0-573f-86d5-78dc5a838d01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290127} {:answer/id #uuid "29edcf7a-d35c-52b8-8e38-5158d1a41364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{3/2}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290128} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6665cd-a133-5366-afad-eabdd2079dc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={({x}^{3}+K)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290129} {:answer/id #uuid "e22ef35d-34a4-5f3c-a3ec-d86527c65c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+K)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290130} {:answer/id #uuid "b01cf114-a799-526b-8b1b-e8c4da11eb05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e22ef35d-34a4-5f3c-a3ec-d86527c65c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+K)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290130} :answer-field/id #uuid "6690658b-b239-5044-8d25-02709b2ca58d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6da6b3d2-c0db-5d2c-8ab4-8655fe604ab1" :question/math-academy-id "q-79665" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,{y}^{′}=1$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}{y}^{′} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2{y}^{1/2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n2{y}^{1/2}=\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{1/2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C \\\\ {y}^{1/2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{C}{2} \\\\ y & ={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{C}{2})}^{2} \\\\ y & ={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+K)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\frac{C}{2}.$"}]}
